.TH LINUX-PLATFORM-REPORT 1 "October 2026" "SASD Freeware M8.5.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
linux-platform-report \- report conservative Linux distribution identity
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B linux-platform-report
.RB [ --input " FILE|-" ]
.RB [ --null ]
.RB [ --version ]
.RB [ --help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read a bounded os-release snapshot without evaluating shell syntax. Native
Linux acquisition prefers /etc/os-release and falls back to /usr/lib/os-release
only if the former is absent. An explicit input file (or stdin) enables offline
replay on other operating systems.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --input " FILE|-"
Read a regular non-symlink fixture file or use a dash for stdin.
.TP
.B --null
Emit seven NUL-terminated fields with no header.
.TP
.B --version
Print utility version.
.TP
.B --help
Print usage and exit.
.SH OUTPUT
TSV columns are SOURCE, ID, ID_LIKE, VERSION_ID, FAMILY, EVIDENCE,
VERSION_MODE. This report is not a package-manager, firewall or support-status
probe. Family hints from ID_LIKE can be ambiguous and are never presented as
installed capabilities.
.SH LIMITS
64 KiB input, at most 512 lines, at most 4096 bytes per line. No partial
report is printed for malformed snapshots. No root privileges or mutations.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Validated snapshot.
.TP
.B 2
Bad arguments.
.TP
.B 3
Unsafe, inaccessible, oversized or invalid input; unsupported native OS.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR os-release (5),
.BR firewall-config-audit (1)
.SH AUTHORS
SASD SysAdmin contributors.
